## How It All Fits Together

Here's a visual flow of how a request travels through the system:

```
Client Request (e.g., POST /books)
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  express.json()     │  ← Parses JSON body into req.body
└─────────┬───────────┘
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  requestLogger      │  ← Logs method, URL, and response time
└─────────┬───────────┘
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  bookRoutes (POST)  │  ← Validates input, calls createBook()
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ├── Success → res.json({ success: true, data: newBook })
          │
          └── Error   → throw new ValidationError(...)
                          │
                          ▼
                ┌─────────────────────┐
                │  errorHandler       │  ← Catches error, sends JSON response
                └─────────────────────┘
```

Every piece is intentionally separated so you can understand, modify, or replace each layer independently — the hallmark of maintainable software architecture.

