# REST API for Book Management — Verbose Educational Example

## Overview

This project implements a fully functional RESTful API for managing books using **Node.js** with the **Express.js** framework. The design follows standard HTTP conventions (GET for reads, POST for creation, PUT for full updates, DELETE for removal) and uses an in-memory array as its data store — ideal for learning because it requires no external database setup while still demonstrating real API patterns. Every function is documented with JSDoc, custom error classes enforce consistent error responses, and the middleware layer handles validation and errors centrally. The code is organized into logical sections (server setup, routes, middleware) to mirror how production APIs are structured, making this a strong foundation for understanding web service architecture.

