Below you'll find a complete, well‑documented Express.js REST API that manages books in memory. The implementation follows REST conventions, uses async/await throughout (even though storage is synchronous), and includes custom error handling, input validation, and comprehensive JSDoc comments. Each file is explained in detail so you can understand *why* each pattern was chosen.

