## Summary of Key Patterns Used

| Pattern | Implementation | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **REST conventions** | Correct HTTP methods + status codes (200/201/204/400/404) | Industry standard; clients expect predictable behavior |
| **Custom error classes** | `AppError` → `NotFoundError`, `ValidationError`, `InternalError` | Structured metadata enables consistent error responses |
| **Global error middleware** | `(err, req, res, next)` as last middleware | Catches all errors in one place; prevents crashes |
| **Validation middleware** | Separate `validateBookBody` / `validateQueryParams` | Keeps routes focused on business logic |
| **In-memory array store** | `books.js` with CRUD functions | Educational simplicity; easy to swap for a DB later |
| **UUID generation** | `uuidv4()` for book IDs | Prevents ID enumeration attacks |
| **JSDoc documentation** | Every function and endpoint documented | Self-documenting code; works with IDE tooltips |
| **Separate route files** | `src/routes/books.js` | Scalable architecture; easy to add new resources |

