## Design Decisions

### REST Conventions
- Used proper HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Consistent URL structure with resource-based endpoints
- Appropriate HTTP status codes (200, 201, 204, 400, 404, 500)

### Async/Await Pattern
- Used synchronous operations for in-memory storage (no database needed)
- Prepared code structure for easy migration to async database operations
- Demonstrates how async/await would be used with real databases

### Error Handling
- Custom error classes provide specific error types
- Global error-handling middleware ensures consistent responses
- Validation errors include field-specific messages

### Middleware Architecture
- Separation of concerns: validation, logging, CORS, error handling
- Middleware runs in sequence for each request
- Easy to add new middleware without modifying existing code

## Environment Variables

