## 📄 `README.md` — Setup & Usage Guide

```markdown
# 📚 Book REST API

A simple, educational REST API built with Node.js and Express.js for managing books.

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Prerequisites
- Node.js 18+ installed
- npm or yarn package manager

### Installation

```bash
# Clone or navigate to the project directory
cd book-api

# Install dependencies (Express is the only dependency)
npm install

# Start the development server
npm start
```

The API will be available at **http://localhost:3000**

## 📖 API Endpoints

All endpoints are prefixed with `/api/v1/books`.

### List All Books
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books
```

### Filter Books
```bash
# By genre
curl "http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books?genre=Fiction"

# By minimum rating
curl "http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books?minRating=4.0"

# Combined filters
curl "http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books?author=hawking&publishedAfter=1960"
```

### Get Single Book
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books/1
```

### Create a New Book
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "Brave New World",
    "author": "Aldous Huxley",
    "genre": "Dystopian",
    "publishedYear": 1932,
    "rating": 4.3
  }'
```

### Update a Book (Full Replace)
```bash
curl -X PUT http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books/1 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "The Great Gatsby",
    "author": "F. Scott Fitzgerald",
    "genre": "Fiction",
    "publishedYear": 1925,
    "rating": 4.5
  }'
```

### Delete a Book
```bash
curl -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books/2
```

### Get Statistics
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/api/v1/books/stats
```

