## 🔑 Key Design Decisions Summary

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **In-memory array** | Simple for education; easy to understand and debug |
| **Separate route/data/error files** | Separation of concerns — each file has one responsibility |
| **Custom error classes with `statusCode`** | Eliminates switch/if chains in the error handler |
| **Consistent JSON envelope `{ success, data/error }`** | Clients can uniformly check `success` to branch logic |
| **Async/await in routes** | Prepares code for eventual database integration |
| **PUT = full replacement** | Follows REST semantics; PATCH would be needed for partial updates |
| **201 Created on POST** | Standard HTTP status for resource creation |
| **Query parameter filtering** | Keeps the list endpoint flexible without extra routes |

Run `npm start` and explore each endpoint with curl or Postman as shown in the README!

